+<!doctype html><html><head><title>Product page cache</title><style>
+body{margin:0;padding:2px 0 0}
+h1{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 4px} .sub{color:var(--muted-foreground);font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:14px}
+.opts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}
+.opt{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:12px 14px;background:var(--card)}
+.opt h2{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 8px} .pick{color:var(--success);font-size:12px;font-weight:500;margin-left:6px}
+table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px} td{padding:5px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)} td+td{text-align:right;font-family:var(--font-mono,ui-monospace)}
+.bad{color:var(--destructive)} .good{color:var(--success)}
+p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:12px 0 0;line-height:1.5}
+</style></head><body>
+<h1>Product page cache: Redis or SQLite</h1>
+<div class="sub">storefront · 3 app servers · measured on staging, 2,000 product pages</div>
+<div class="opts">
+<div class="opt"><h2>Redis<span class="pick">recommended</span></h2><table>
+<tr><td>Hit rate</td><td class="good">94%</td></tr>
+<tr><td>p95 page render</td><td class="good">41 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Copies of each page</td><td>1</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Price change clears</td><td>1 key</td></tr>
+<tr><td>New servers to run</td><td>0, staging has one</td></tr></table></div>
+<div class="opt"><h2>SQLite</h2><table>
+<tr><td>Hit rate</td><td class="bad">38%</td></tr>
+<tr><td>p95 page render</td><td>212 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Copies of each page</td><td>3</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Price change clears</td><td class="bad">3 files</td></tr>
+<tr><td>New servers to run</td><td class="good">0</td></tr></table></div>
+</div>
+<p>Each app server keeps its own SQLite file, so a page cached on one is a miss on the other two, and a price change has to be cleared three times.</p>
+</body></html>
